{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>ונודעה</b> — bet. ונודעה החטאת ונודעה יד ה' את עבדיו וזעם את אויביו — that even for inadvertent sin for which one must bring a sin-offering and does not bring it, the Holy One, blessed be He, exacts punishment from him. And this is: ונודעה יד ה' את עבדיו — one who sinned and brings an offering; וזעם את — one who does not bring it." "<b>והביאו אותו</b> לפני אהל מועד. Four times in the Masorah: here, and elsewhere: והביאו אבנים אחרות — regarding the metzora; והביאו בניך בחוצן; והביאו את כל אחיכם. One who is obligated to bring an offering to HaShem and does not bring it to the kohen — in the end the kohen must come to see the plague of his house. And if he does bring it, he merits what is stated: והביאו בניך בחוצן and והביאו אל כל אחיכם מכל וגו'."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The lemma reads ונורעה (a form that does not occur in the biblical text), likely a variant or scribal error for ונודעה; translated as written. The juxtaposition alludes to Isaiah 66:14 (ונודעה יד ה' את עבדיו) and Isaiah 66:15 (וזעם את אויביו), though no verse addresses are given in the source.", 1 "The first Masorah citation והביאו אבנים אחרות corresponds to Leviticus 14:42 (regarding the metzora's house). The third, והביאו בניך בחוצן, likely alludes to Isaiah 66:20 (והביאו את כל אחיכם); the citation as written may be a conflation or variant. The fourth, והביאו את כל אחיכם לו, also appears to reference Isaiah 66:20. No verse addresses are given in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:56.107128629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}